True, but it is worth noting that the last three are noticeably more 
rare to find, and the first one of each of those needs to be used for 
the alchemy against the rest of the potions.  Plus, you need three
potions to make 'saving' one from each stack actually increase the
number of healing potions you get:

Start with 5 potions of healing + 2 potions of speed.

* Dip 4 potions of healing into 1 potion of speed = 4 EH potions.
* Dip 1 potion of speed into 1 potion of healing = 1 EH, 5 total.
--
* Dip 5 potions of healing into 1 potion of speed = 5 EH potions, and
you still have a single potion of speed left.

Contrast with 5 healing, 3 speed:

* 4 healing into 1 speed = 4 EH potions.
* 2 speed into 1 healing = 2 EH potions, 6 total.
--
* 5 healing into 1 speed = 5 EH potions and 2 speed left.

Also, gain level and speed do have uses later in the game; gain level
for cursing, and speed so you can avoid wearing speed boots in some
circumstances.  While you certainly _can_ use these for full healing, I
think most players would prefer not to, leaving only the occasional
spare gain energy that could be mix-n-matched if you found 3; given gain
energy's rarity, i'm not sure this is something worth counting on.

